{"type": "FeatureCollection", "_comment": "Subscription zones for the flasher's location step. Each feature carries a 'code'; a feature with a 'parent' is a zone nested inside that state, and the most specific match wins. Codes are DATA -- the naming convention is not settled, so nothing in the page hardcodes one. States come from region-map/data/gc-states.geojson. us-al-mob is Mobile + Baldwin counties (US Census, FIPS 01097 + 01003) dissolved into one outline, buffered 300 m and clipped to the Florida line: that dataset's coastline runs ~200 m inland of Orange Beach, which otherwise fell outside its own county. The county set is clipped to land, so Mobile Bay belongs to neither county; it is filled back in, since the real county line runs down the middle of the bay.", "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"code": "us-al", "name": "Alabama"}, "geometry": {"type": "Polygon", "coordinates": [[[-87.3593, 35.0012], [-85.6067, 34.9847], [-85.4314, 34.1249], [-85.185, 32.8597], [-85.0699, 32.5804], [-84.9604, 32.4215], [-85.0042, 32.323], [-84.8892, 32.2627], [-85.059, 32.1367], [-85.0535, 32.0108], [-85.1411, 31.841], [-85.0426, 31.5398], [-85.1138, 31.2769], [-85.0042, 31.003], [-85.4971, 30.9975], [-87.6003, 30.9975], [-87.6331, 30.8661], [-87.4086, 30.6744], [-87.4469, 30.5101], [-87.3702, 30.4279], [-87.5181, 30.2801], [-87.6551, 30.2472], [-87.907, 30.4115], [-87.9344, 30.658], [-88.0111, 30.6854], [-88.1042, 30.4991], [-88.137, 30.3184], [-88.3944, 30.3677], [-88.4711, 31.8958], [-88.2411, 33.7963], [-88.0987, 34.8916], [-88.2027, 34.9957], [-87.3593, 35.0012]]]}}, {"type": "Feature", "properties": {"code": "us-fl", "name": "Florida"}, "geometry": {"type": "Polygon", "coordinates": [[[-85.4971, 30.9975], [-85.0042, 31.003], [-84.8673, 30.7127], [-83.4981, 30.647], [-82.2164, 30.5703], [-82.1672, 30.3567], [-82.0467, 30.3622], [-82.0028, 30.5649], [-82.0412, 30.7511], [-81.9481, 30.8278], [-81.718, 30.7456], [-81.4442, 30.7073], [-81.384, 30.2746], [-81.2